# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Files in public/ are copied to the static export output root (out/),
# so this file ships to the deployment root where Cloudflare Pages reads it.
#
# Use this file for PATH-based redirects only, e.g.:
#   /old-path   /new-path        301
#   /blog/*     /posts/:splat    301
#
# IMPORTANT: hostname/domain-level redirects are NOT supported here.
# Cloudflare Pages matches the source against the request PATH only, and the
# rule applies to ALL hostnames on the project (so a bare "/*" rule would loop
# on the canonical domain). To forward zero-to-ai.pages.dev -> zero-to-ai.dev,
# configure a dashboard Redirect Rule (Rules -> Redirect Rules) that matches
# Hostname == "zero-to-ai.pages.dev". See:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/rules/url-forwarding/single-redirects/
